%% 13.4 Team shuffle & fixture generation (preparation)
%% Source of truth for this diagram. Rendered from ../specs/2026-07-28-kickr-spec-v2-changes.md §13.4
%% Edit here, not in the spec — the spec links to this file.
%%
%% SUPERSEDED for implementation detail. The events feature spec revised this:
%% the CLIENT now shuffles and submits the roster via PUT /events/:id/teams,
%% and POST /shuffle is a server-side fallback on the same write path. See
%% ./events-5-4-team-submission-fixtures.mmd for what was actually built.
%% Kept because §13.4 of the parent spec still links here.
sequenceDiagram
    actor O as Organizer
    participant API as Events/Shuffle
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant CH as Chat
    participant N as Notifications

    O->>API: PATCH /events/:id/status {preparation}
    API->>API: assert legal transition + organizer
    API-->>O: status = preparation

    Note over O,API: REVISED — the client now shuffles and submits<br/>PUT /events/:id/teams. POST /shuffle below is<br/>the server-side fallback. Both share one path.

    O->>API: POST /events/:id/shuffle
    API->>API: reject unless status == preparation
    API->>DB: load EventPlayers (status: joined)
    API->>API: Fisher-Yates → deal across colour teams
    API->>DB: bulkWrite EventPlayer.team

    API->>API: generate double round-robin matches[]
    API->>DB: save Event.matches (scores null)
    Note over API: every N >= 2 gets fixtures —<br/>2 teams play twice, 4 teams play 12

    API->>CH: upsert EventTeamChat per team
    API->>N: notify each player of their team
    API-->>O: { teams, fixtures, unassignedPlayerIds }

    Note over API,DB: fixtures lock once the event leaves preparation —<br/>resubmitting inside it regenerates them wholesale
